  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=2$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=4x\\,{y}^{2}-(16x+3)y+(16x+6).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(x)={z}^{\u2032}(x)+{y}_{0}^{\u2032}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=2.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{\u2032}(x)=0$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+2\\,\u21d2\\,{y}^{\u2032}={z}^{\u2032}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{\u2032}=4x(z+2)^{2}-(16x+3)(z+2)+(16x+6).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{\u2032} & =4x(z+2)^{2}-(16x+3)(z+2)+(16x+6) \\\\ {z}^{\u2032} & =4x{z}^{2}-3z \\\\ {z}^{\u2032}+3z & =4x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=3,\\,Q(x)=4x,\\,n=2.\n$$",
